+## Known issue: zero-byte thumbnails
+
+`render.py` carries a `time.sleep(2)` before the upload. It suppresses a
+1-in-40 zero-byte-object rate in staging by an unidentified mechanism, and
+the suppression itself is unconfirmed. `docs/zero-byte-thumbnails.md` records
+what is confirmed, what is ruled out (source truncation is), and what a
+staging run needs to log to settle it. Read it before touching `render.py`
+or reasoning about zero-byte or missing thumbnails.
